    ("VendingMachineTankDispenserEngineering", "A vendor for dispensing gas tanks. This one has an engineering livery."),
    ("VendingMachineTheater", "A vending machine containing costumes."),
    ("VendingMachineVendomat", "Only the finest robust equipment in space!"),
    ("VendingMachineViroDrobe", "An unsterilized machine for dispending virology related clothing."),
    ("VendingMachineWallMedical", "It's a wall-mounted medical equipment dispenser. Natural chemicals only!"),
    ("VendingMachineWallMedicalCivilian", "It's a wall-mounted medical equipment dispenser. Natural chemicals only!"),
    ("VendingMachineWinter", "The best place to enjoy the cold!"),
    ("VendingMachineYouTool", "A vending machine containing standard tools. A label reads: Tools for tools."),
    ("ViolaInstrument", "Like a violin, but worse."),
    ("ViolinInstrument", "The favorite of musical virtuosos and bluegrass bands."),
    ("WantedListCartridge", "A program to get a list of wanted persons."),
    ("WardenIDCard", "A card necessary to access various areas aboard the station."),
    ("WardenPDA", "The OS appears to have been jailbroken."),
    ("WardrobeChapelFilled", "You have to look presentable for your flock."),
    ("WardrobeGreyFilled", "A wardrobe packed with a tide of grey clothing."),
    ("WardrobePrisonFilled", "Contains a selection of nice orange clothes for people enjoying their stay in the brig."),
    ("WardrobeRoboticsFilled", "You can build a robot out of this locker."),
    ("WardrobeWhite", "A wardrobe packed with stylish white clothing."),
    ("WaterVaporCanister", "A canister that can contain any type of gas. This one is supposed to contain water vapor. It can be attached to connector ports using a wrench."),
    ("WeaponAntiqueLaser", "This is an antique laser pistol. All craftsmanship is of the highest quality. It is decorated with a mahogany grip and chrome filigree. The object menaces with spikes of energy. On the item is an image of a captain and a clown. The clown is dead. The captain is striking a heroic pose."),
    ("WeaponCapacitorRecharger", "A modern recharging station that can fit both power cells and small electronic devices."),
    ("WeaponCrusher", "An early design of the proto-kinetic accelerator."),
    ("WeaponCrusherDagger", "A scaled down version of a proto-kinetic crusher. Uses kinetic energy to vibrate the blade at high speeds."),
    ("WeaponCrusherGlaive", "An early design of the proto-kinetic accelerator, in glaive form. Provides better healing in exchange for less charged damage."),
    ("WeaponDisabler", "A self-defense weapon that exhausts organic targets, weakening them until they collapse."),
    ("WeaponEnergyMagnum", "A high powered self-charging energy pistol designed for elite security personnel. It has has three firing modes allowing for either high damage, window piercing, or non-lethal disabling."),
    ("WeaponFlareGun", "A compact, single-shot pistol that fires shotgun shells. Comes with a safety feature that prevents the user from fitting lethal shells inside."),
    ("WeaponLaserCarbine", "Favoured by Nanotrasen Security for being cheap and easy to use."),
    ("WeaponMeleeNeedle", "A specialty weapon used in the destruction of unique syndicate morale-boosting equipment."),
    ("WeaponPistolMk58", "Designed by Nanotrasen’s Small Arms Division, the Mk58 is a conventional semi-automatic pistol with a simple recoil-operated action and excellent reliability. The standard sidearm of Nanotrasen’s station security and emergency response teams. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines."),
    ("WeaponProtoKineticAccelerator", "Fires low-damage kinetic bolts at a short range."),
    ("WeaponRevolverDeckard", "A beautifully machined, custom-built revolver. Used when there is no time for the Voight-Kampff test. Loads 5 rounds of .45 magnum."),
    ("WeaponRifleFoam", "A premium foam rifle of the highest quality. Its plastic feels rugged, and its mechanisms sturdy."),
    ("WeaponRifleLecter", "Popular gas-operated combat rifle used heavily by Nanotrasen and SolGov. Operating in semi or fully automatic, its accuracy, stopping power, and reliability make it excel in all manner of environments. Feeds from .20 rifle magazines."),
    ("WeaponShotgunDoubleBarreledRubber", "An immortal classic. Uses .50 shotgun shells."),
    ("WeaponShotgunKammerer", "An old yet faithful design, and a favorite among irregular forces of many worlds. Uses .50 shotgun shells."),
    ("WeaponSniperMosin", "A true relic, the Kardashev-Mosin has served in nearly every armed conflict since its creation 670 years ago. The bolt-action design of the rifle remains virtually identical to its original design, whether used for hunting, sniping, or endless trench warfare. Loads 10 rounds of .30 rifle."),
    ("WeaponStickyHand", "They're saying you're reaching. They're saying it's a stretch. You'll show them all, and you'll stick it to them."),
    ("WeaponSubMachineGunDrozd", "A modern SMG manufactured by Nanotrasen’s Small Arms Division. It features an exceptional rate of fire in burst mode, useful for holding defensive angles or engaging hostiles at longer ranges. Feeds from .35 SMG magazines."),
    ("WeaponSubMachineGunWt550", "A truly unique firearm, the WT550 was designed by Nanotrasen's Small Arms Division as a compact submachine gun fully controllable with one hand. It contains an exotic internal recoil buffer and feeds from special top-mounted .35 magazines."),
    ("WeaponWaterBlaster", "With this bad boy, you'll be the coolest kid at the summer barbecue."),
    ("WeaponWaterPistol", "The dinkiest of water-based weaponry. You swear the trigger doesn't do anything."),
    ("WeedSpray", "It's a toxic mixture, in spray form, to kill small weeds."),
    ("Welder", "Melts anything as long as it's fueled, don't forget your eye protection!"),
    ("WelderIndustrial", "An industrial welder with over double the fuel capacity."),
    ("WelderIndustrialAdvanced", "An advanced industrial welder with over double the fuel capacity and hotter flame."),
    ("WelderMini", "A miniature welder used during emergencies."),
    ("WetFloorSign", "Caution! Wet Floor!"),
    ("Whistle", "Someone forgot to turn off a kettle?"),
    ("WhoopieCushion", "A practical joke device involving flatulence humour."),
    ("WireBrush", "A bristly steel wire brush, perfect for scraping away even the toughest patches of rust."),
    ("Wirecutter", "This kills the wire."),
    ("Wrench", "A common tool for assembly and disassembly. Remember: lefty latchy, righty removey."),
    ("Wristwatch", "A cheap watch for telling time. How much did you waste playing Space Station 14?"),
    ("WristwatchGold", "A fancy watch worth more than your kidney. It was owned by the notorious Syndicate mobster Vunibaldo \"200 Pound Horse Meat Grinder\" Frediani."),
    ("XenoBasherGlass", "A metamorphic glass that automagically turns into a glass appropriate for the drink within. There's a sanded off patent number on the bottom."),
    ("XylophoneInstrument", "Rainbow colored glockenspiel."),
    ("Zipties", "Tough single-use plastic zipties, ideal for restraining rowdy prisoners."),
    ("d20Dice", "A die with twenty sides. The preferred die to throw at the GM."),
    ("d6Dice", "A die with six sides. Basic and serviceable."),
    ("d8Dice", "A die with eight sides. It feels... lucky."),
]
